node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored here, unlike the MCP server repos in this
# project. Those publish to npm, so the registry carries their build output.
# This one is GitHub-only, and the built bundle IS the deliverable - the file
# the site copies into its assets. Ignoring it would leave the thing this repo
# exists to produce obtainable only by cloning and building it.

# The vendored binary is regenerated byte-for-byte by `npm run vendor` from a
# pinned devDependency, so committing it here as well as in dist/ would put the
# same 653KB in the repo twice. The vendored GLUE is committed, because that is
# code a person should be able to read and diff against upstream; the binary is
# not, because nobody can read it either way.
vendor/*.wasm
